      content:
        "\n# Where to start: a 5-minute guide to getting your finances in order\n\nTracking your money doesn't have to be complicated. This guide walks you through the first steps — in five minutes and without budgets for now.\n\n## Why track first\n\nA budget set without real data rarely sticks. Logging one or two weeks of spending shows you where the money goes before you decide how much to allocate.\n\n- **Week 1–2:** Just record. Don't limit, just observe.\n- **Week 3:** Look at totals by category and decide what to adjust.\n\n## A seven-day plan\n\nA gentle seven-day start — no streaks, no penalties for missed days.\n\n### Day 1: Log a recent purchase\n\nOpen DuoBalance and log a recent purchase — coffee, groceries, transit. It takes seconds.\n\n### Day 2–3: Add two more\n\nAdd one or two expenses per day. You'll see your balances update and categories take shape.\n\n### Day 4–5: Invite your partner\n\nFrom Settings → Household members you can invite your partner. Do a monthly review together, not a per-purchase check.\n\n### Day 6–7: Observe, don't judge\n\nAt the end of the week, open Reports and look at your totals. Just observe — this isn't the moment to fix everything.\n\n## What to ignore for now\n\nFor these two weeks you can ignore the Budget tab. Creating limits without data is guessing. Come back when you have real numbers.\n\n## Next step\n\nWhen you have a week of data, read how to [read your first month](/guide/read-your-first-month) — but only if you finished this guide. No rush.\n",
